{
  "case_id": "2021-21-954",
  "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Argued April 26, 2022\u2014Decided June 30, 2022"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The States of Texas and Missouri (respondents) brought suit in the Northern District of Texas against the Secretary and others, asserting that the June 1 Memorandum violated the INA and the Administrative Procedure Act (APA)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts delivered the opinion of the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question, then, is whether section 1252(f)(1) strips the lower courts of subject matter jurisdiction over these claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the theory works both ways. Congress conferred contiguous-territory return authority in expressly discretionary terms. \u201c `[M]ay return the alien' means `may return the alien.' \u201d The desire to redress the Government's purported violation of section 1225(b)(2)(A) does not justify transforming the nature of the authority conferred by section 1225(b)(2)(C)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the availability of the parole option additionally makes clear that the Court of Appeals erred in holding that the INA required the Government to continue implementing MPP."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government was correct in Jennings and is wrong here. \u201c[S]hall be detained\u201d means \u201cshall be detained.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority claims that the Government's use of its parole authority under \u00a7 1182(d)(5)(A) is not before us, ante, at 807, but the Government cites that authority as a reason why it does not need to use its contiguous-territory return authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is nothing strange about this interpretation of how the relevant provisions of the INA work together."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority's main reason for rejecting the argument just described is that the contiguous-return provision does not say expressly that it was meant to \u201coperate as a mandatory cure of any noncompliance with the Government's detention obligations.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Constitution gives Congress broad authority to set immigration policy. See Art. I, \u00a7 8, cl. 4."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As I see it, the Government's litigation tactic\u2014fling the October 29 Memoranda with a suggestion of mootness but without seeking to dismiss its appeal\u2014could have triggered one of four responses from the Court of Appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Administrative order terminating MPP could not provide a ground for vacating the injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With these three options off the table, the Fifth Circuit reasonably chose the fourth option."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0004-0010",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with the Court's analysis of the merits\u2014but not with its decision to reach them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the normal course, we would vacate and remand this case for further proceedings in light of Aleman Gonzalez. Instead, the Court plows ahead to break new jurisdictional ground. Acting on a compressed timeline, it embraces a theory of \u00a7 1252(f)(1) that\u2014so far as I can tell\u2014no court of appeals has ever adopted: that \u00a7 1252(f)(1) limits only the lower courts' remedial authority, not their subject-matter jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0005-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have several doubts about the Court's analysis of \u00a7 1252(f)(1). To begin with, the Court assumes that we face an either/or choice between subject-matter jurisdiction and remedial authority, with the former being only about a court's authority to decide merits questions and the latter being only about the relief a court can grant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6617eaffedbd3ab78aaf1c20e6ce2821c93efbe806d5060e90156953c198be76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6617eaffedbd-0005-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Indeed, the Court explicitly chooses not to opine on some of the issues that might help explain the parenthetical's unusual reservation."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
